PURPOSE Preserve completed actions, ongoing execution and accepted service.
INPUT previous feasible Plan, new model, implementation time
OUTPUT fixed prefix, residual state and required-service constraints
REFERENCES DynConstrGenerater.Generating_Dy_Constr; periodic rescheduling framework

PROCEDURE SnapshotCommittedState(previous,implementationTime)
    REQUIRE previous is a validated Plan
    completedPrefix := actions completed before or at implementationTime
    inProgressArcs := selected actions with departure < implementationTime < arrival
    include any issued noncancelable action from the execution/dispatch interface
    FOR each physical vehicle k
        if k has an ongoing/noncancelable action
            residualSources[k] := that action's final state and release time
        else
            residualSources[k] := its reached state at implementationTime
        derive onboard order IDs from completed/committed pickup, transfer and drop
    acceptedUnfinishedOrders := previous.acceptedOrders minus completed deliveries
    retain their current carrier, location, service state and promised requirements
    return DynamicState{previousPlan:previous,implementationTime,completedPrefix,
                        inProgressArcs,residualSources,onboardOrders,
                        acceptedUnfinishedOrders}

PROCEDURE FreezeLegacyDecisions(previous,newModel,ImT)
    state := SnapshotCommittedState(previous,ImT)
    IF newModel uses full-horizon variables
        FOR every prior arc whose execution is completed/committed
            if its completed package owner is absent from the new demand model
                retain it in immutable committed history; continue
            match by catalog-independent stable owner/record/state/time identity
            REQUIRE exactly one matching variable
            fix its new Y to the prior selected value
        fix each selected in-progress/noncancelable action to 1 through its arrival
        disallow alternative departures that conflict with a fixed action
        forbid newly introduced arcs departing before the relevant released state
    ELSE IF newModel uses a residual suffix
        replace each vehicle source by state.residualSources[k]
        initialize package sources and onboard loads from the same state
        retain the fixed prefix outside the residual optimization objective
        reduce each remaining duty allowance by committed duration
    FOR each accepted unfinished order r
        prohibit its unserved route
        require all still-unperformed service and promised delivery-window events
        preserve its current carrier until a legal future transfer
    fix completed delivery/transfer events so they cannot be repeated or undone
    attach state to newModel; mark commitmentsApplied to avoid duplicate insertion
    return newModel

PROCEDURE CheckCommitments(candidate,state)
    REQUIRE identical completed/ongoing/noncancelable actions
    REQUIRE suffix departure state/time equals the fixed prefix's release state/time
    REQUIRE onboard membership and transfer carrier balance match at the boundary
    REQUIRE every previously accepted unfinished order remains served
    return valid or a commitment diagnostic

NOTES
    Full-horizon and residual encodings are alternatives. Use one consistently,
    preserve ongoing actions and onboard loads, and count committed cost/time once.
    FreezeLegacyDecisions retains its function name for call-site compatibility.
